    "explanation": "The law of demand, a fundamental principle in economics, stipulates that an increase in the price of a commodity, holding all other factors constant, results in a decrease in the quantity demanded. This relationship reflects the typical behavior of consumers in the marketplace. When the price of a product rises, consumers tend to adjust their purchasing behavior by buying less of that particular item. The rationale behind this is often rooted in the idea that higher prices reduce the affordability of the product, prompting consumers to seek alternatives or cut back on their consumption. Thus, the law of demand plays a crucial role in understanding and predicting consumer behavior in response to changes in price levels.",
