    "explanation": "When the selling price set by a monopolist falls below their short-run marginal cost, it indicates that the monopolist is operating at a loss. In this scenario, the revenue generated from sales is insufficient to cover the production costs, including the short-run marginal cost. This situation is economically unsustainable for the monopolist, as they are incurring losses on each unit produced and sold. In the short run, a monopolist may continue operating at a loss, but in the long run, such a situation is untenable, and adjustments may be necessary, such as price increases or cost-cutting measures, to restore profitability and cover both variable and fixed costs.",
