    "explanation": "One of the criticisms of the price mechanism is that it can lead to a widening of the inequitable gap between the rich and the poor. This is because the price mechanism does not take into account the distribution of income or wealth. As a result, the rich are able to buy more goods and services than the poor, even if the poor need them more. For example, if the price of food increases, the rich will still be able to buy food, but the poor may not be able to afford to buy as much food. This can lead to malnutrition and other health problems for the poor. In addition, the price mechanism can lead to a concentration of wealth in the hands of a few people. This is because the rich are able to use their wealth to buy assets, such as stocks and bonds, which can appreciate in value. As a result, the rich get richer, while the poor get poorer.",
